  "id": "Compound::DB00535 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Cefdinir, a cephalosporin antibiotic, is linked to Slc15a1 through a shared pathway involving cephalosporin antibiotics. The evidence suggests that Cefdinir, as part of the cephalosporin class, binds to Slc15a1 via its interaction with Ceftizoxime or Cefuroxime, which are also included in the cephalosporin family. This indicates a potential mechanism where the structural similarity of cephalosporins allows them to interact with Slc15a1, possibly through a common binding site or functional domain. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores supports the idea that Cefdinir's interaction with Slc15a1 is mediated by its classification within the cephalosporin class, which in turn binds to Slc15a1. The recurring theme of cephalosporin antibiotics as intermediaries between Cefdinir and Slc15a1 highlights a possible functional relationship rooted in pharmacological classification and molecular interaction.",
